adjudication.rationale:
In `reauthenticationOfUserWithoutPasskey()` the diff adds blocks like:
```java
try {
  MatcherAssert.assertThat(driver.findElement(By.xpath("//form[@id='webauth']")), nullValue());
  fail("Not expected to have webauthn button");
} catch (Exception nsee) {
  // expected
}
```
This does correctly fail if the element exists (the `assertThat(..., nullValue())` would throw an `AssertionError`, which is not caught by `catch (Exception)`), but it will also treat *any* `Exception` from `findElement` (stale element, WebDriver failures, etc.) as “expected”. That can mask intermittent Selenium issues and make the test falsely pass when it should signal infrastructure/DOM problems. This is a test-quality/robustness concern, not an application behavior bug.
